  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Born in Istanbul, Dinçkök studied business administration at Boston University before entering the family group in 1994. He began in purchasing at textile producer Ak-Al, then moved to a coordinating role at power producer Akenerji. Those assignments gave him operating experience across two of Akkök Holding’s established sectors before he progressed to its board and executive committee.\n\nDinçkök now chairs Akkök Holding and several important portfolio companies, including acrylic-fibre producer Aksa Akrilik, chemicals manufacturer Akkim and property company Akiş REIT. His career represents the third-generation stewardship of a group founded by his grandfather, Raif Dinçkök. Under his leadership, the group remains centred on advanced materials, chemicals, energy and commercial property, with a substantial industrial workforce and international sales.",
    "html": "<p>Born in Istanbul, Dinçkök studied business administration at Boston University before entering the family group in 1994. He began in purchasing at textile producer Ak-Al, then moved to a coordinating role at power producer Akenerji. Those assignments gave him operating experience across two of Akkök Holding’s established sectors before he progressed to its board and executive committee.</p>\r\n<p>Dinçkök now chairs Akkök Holding and several important portfolio companies, including acrylic-fibre producer Aksa Akrilik, chemicals manufacturer Akkim and property company Akiş REIT. His career represents the third-generation stewardship of a group founded by his grandfather, Raif Dinçkök. Under his leadership, the group remains centred on advanced materials, chemicals, energy and commercial property, with a substantial industrial workforce and international sales.</p>\r\n",
